### Lesson 19 — Task 19.4 Posts API
### VS Code: install "REST Client" (humao.rest-client), then click "Send Request" above each block.
### Run first, from backend/: node --watch exercises/antonyshisia/posts-api.js

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Get all posts
GET {{base}}/api/posts

### Get a single post
GET {{base}}/api/posts/1

### Filter by author (case-insensitive, partial match)
GET {{base}}/api/posts?author=jane

### Newest first
GET {{base}}/api/posts?sort=newest

### Most liked first
GET {{base}}/api/posts?sort=popular

### Missing post -> 404
GET {{base}}/api/posts/99

### Create a post
POST {{base}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Query Strings vs Route Params",
  "content": "Params name the thing. Query strings filter the list.",
  "author": "Alex Kim"
}

### Missing fields -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Untitled"
}

### Update a post
PUT {{base}}/api/posts/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Getting Started with Node.js and Express",
  "content": "Node.js is a JavaScript runtime that pairs well with Express."
}

### Update a missing post -> 404
PUT {{base}}/api/posts/99
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Does not exist"
}

### Like a post
PATCH {{base}}/api/posts/2/like

### Like a missing post -> 404
PATCH {{base}}/api/posts/99/like

### Delete a post -> 204
DELETE {{base}}/api/posts/1

### Delete a missing post -> 404
DELETE {{base}}/api/posts/1
